# W30b, b (k10). First, with nothing running, its own trip to dng205b2, where its gate disc takes it home and sets its
# return mat (GATESTAGE) to dng205b2. Then, while a's Dry Land instance has never been at dng205b2, the lobby's return
# mat puts b there: a NEW of its own (I1a; I1b shows a's row greyed "Story not here yet"); home again, and after a reached
# dng205b2 the next arrival there joins a without leaving a's story.
campaign until stage=stagml11,control
idle until epoch>=@40
explore mate00 until onme:mate00
gate mate00 1 until stage=stag0201,control
explore matz00 yes until stage=stag0202,control
explore matz01 yes until stage=dng205b1,control
explore matz01 yes until stage=dng205b2,control
log b set its return mat
disk 8 until stage=stagml11,control fail epoch>=@350
log b home before a hosts
idle until epoch>=@480
explore mate02 yes until stage=dng205b2,control
log b alone on dng205b2
idle until frames>=300 fail present>=2
disk 8 until stage=stagml11,control
idle until epoch>=@700
explore mate02 yes until stage=dng205b2,control
wander 0 0 30 until present=2,sealed>=600 fail epoch>=@1000
log b joined a on dng205b2
